==Strategy ==

----
* The '''Glitch Toilet''' has a very high amount of HP,  so you should use high DPS units to defeat this enemy. (a cheap one is {{Mythic|[[Future Large Clockman]]}}, ''due to its overpowered time-stop, plus it has some stun-blocks and high, single target DPS.''))
----
* Glitch Toilet is very fast, so you could slow it down to make it easier to defeat. [[Units]] that can slow down this enemy are [[TV Woman]], Green Laser Cameramen or [[Mech Cameraman]]. {{Exclusive|[[TV Woman]]}} is not recommended as it does low damage.
----
* Glitch Toilet will quickly stun units, so you should use [[Medic Cameraman|a Medic Cameraman]], [[Camera Repair Drone]] or [[Speaker Repair Drone]] to unstun the [[Units|units.]]
----
* When Glitch Toilet goes off the track to stun a unit and it quickly gets unstunned, Glitch Toilet will go back to this unit to stun it again. This process will keep repeating, giving your units an alot of time to attack this enemy.
**Alternatively, you can also use [[Shield Cameraman]] to defeat this unit, as Glitch Toilet will keep circling around the Shield Cameraman while taking damage.
----
*Do not place Spider units next to your base. When Glitch Toilet rushes forward to stun a unit, it may use any unit on its way to your base, but it aims for the unit's spawn location. If you place a Spider unit next to your base, Glitch Toilet can rush towards that location and immediately kill the base after finding no unit to stun.
----
*If you dont have [[Shield Cameraman]], it is reccomended to use any inf-stun unit (like {{Legendary|[[Leprechaun Cameraman]]}}, ''as it has a chance to infinitely stun this unit, whilst damaging it) , or a decoy unit (like the {{Basic|[[Toilet]]}}, ''relatively because of its cheap price'') and place it nearby in a area where the '''Glitch Toilet''' is, and atleast almost no units in the area.
----
==Trivia== 
*He is based on the [https://skibidi-toilet.fandom.com/wiki/Glitch_Skibidi_Toilet Glitch Skibidi Toilet.]
*He can go off-track to stun your units.
*When The Glitch Toilet finishes stunning your units it will rush into your base at rapid speed.
*The Glitch Toilet has a similar appearance with the mythic [[Glitch Cameraman]].
*In the series, the Glitch Toilet died in Episode 54 and his toilet was used for [[Ninja Cameraman]].
*This is the first [[Enemies|enemy]] to be a [[:Category:Spawner Minion|Spawner Minion]], because two of it can be spawned when  [[Dual Cargo Toilets]] are destroyed.
